    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hegarty Properties are delighted to present to the market approximately 1.03acres (0.42 hectares) of land in Whitegate, offering a rare opportunity to acquire a rare parcel in a peaceful yet highly accessible East Cork location. Enjoying a private countryside setting, the site combines rural tranquillity with excellent connectivity to surrounding towns and amenities The holding is rich in history with ruins on the site, which once acted as a safe house during the Irish Civil War. This coastal plot offers stunning views over the countryside of the sea. These ruins may qualify for Vacant Property Refurbishment grant derelict top up (subject to conditions).\r\nFramed by mature natural boundaries and enjoying sea views, the property offers both privacy and an exceptional sense of space. The holding does not have any services.\r\nIdeally positioned from Midleton, Whitegate, and Cloyne, the location provides easy access to an excellent range of amenities including schools, shops, cafés, restaurants, sports clubs and everyday services. The renowned East Cork coastline, including Inch Beach and Powerhead Pier, is also within easy reach, offering beaches, cliff walks and a sought-after coastal lifestyle.  The site also allows for easy access to Cork City along the N25 and through the Jack Lynch tunnel\r\nFolio Number: CK122157F\r\nFor sale not subject to planning permission.\r\n\r\n\r\nGUIDE PRICE: €110,000"
      },
